{"name":"Doe","hex":"#b68761","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Doe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname of English origin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Doe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Doe (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Doe were a British indie rock band from London, England, consisting of Nicola Leel, Jake Popyura and Dean Smithers (guitar). The band released two studio albums and toured extensively in the UK, Europe and USA."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Doe_2019.jpg/330px-Doe_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doe_(band)"},{"title":"Pod (The Breeders album)","blocks":[{"text":"Pod is the debut studio album by American alternative rock band the Breeders, released by 4AD records on May 29, 1990. Engineered by Steve Albini, the album features band leader Kim Deal on vocals and guitar, Josephine Wiggs on bass, Britt Walford on drums, and Tanya Donelly on guitar. Albini's production prioritized sound over technical accomplishment; the final takes favor the band's spontaneous live \"in studio\" performances."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3b/The_Breeders_Pod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pod_(The_Breeders_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Kim-Breeders-Zappa-Tel-Aviv-2008-08-22-06.jpg/500px-Kim-Breeders-Zappa-Tel-Aviv-2008-08-22-06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Kim-Breeders-Zappa-Tel-Aviv-2008-08-22-06.jpg/1280px-Kim-Breeders-Zappa-Tel-Aviv-2008-08-22-06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Kim-Breeders-Zappa-Tel-Aviv-20